.TH FERROKEY.YAML 5 "August 2026" "Ferrokey" "Ferrokey Manual"
.SH NAME
ferrokey.yaml \- Ferrokey UI configuration
.SH DESCRIPTION
Configuration for the
.BR ferrokey (1)
on-screen keyboard UI. Every field is optional; missing fields fall back
to the defaults below. The file is loaded from
.IR /etc/ferrokey/ferrokey.yaml ,
then
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/ferrokey/ferrokey.yaml
(or
.IR ~/.config/ferrokey/ferrokey.yaml ),
or from an explicit
.B \-\-config
path.
.PP
Unlike the broker configuration
.RB ( ferrokeyd.yaml (5)),
this file is not a security boundary: the UI is fully unprivileged.
.SH FIELDS
.TP
.B layout
Type: string. Default: "us". The active layout: a builtin id
.RB ( us ,
.RB de ,
.RB fr ,
.RB gb ,
.RB dvorak ,
.RB us-intl ,
...)
or a system xkb spec
.RB ( us(intl) ,
.RB de@neo ,
...).
Validation: unknown ids and unloadable xkb specs abort startup with an
error.
.TP
.B view
Type: string. Default: "compact". The keyboard view:
.BR compact " or " full .
Views are visual arrangements over the same physical-key engine.
Validation: unknown views abort startup.
.TP
.B socket_path
Type: string (path). Default:
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/ferrokeyd.sock
(or
.IR /tmp/ferrokeyd.sock ).
The broker socket the UI connects to.
.TP
.B width ", " height
Type: integer (px). Defaults: 920, 342. Initial OSK size. Validation: must
be > 0.
.TP
.B scale
Type: float. Default: 0.75. Initial uniform keyboard scale: 1.0 is the
view's natural size; the shipped default renders the OSK 25% smaller. The
window can be resized at runtime by dragging its bottom-right corner, which
rescales the whole keyboard (0.35-3.0). Validation: must be in (0, 4].
.TP
.B x11_display
Type: string or null. Default: null. Override the X11 display for the
x11-no-input backend (mainly for tests); null = auto-detect from
.BR DISPLAY .
.TP
.B sticky
Type: map. Sticky modifier behaviour: a quick tap on a modifier latches it
for the next qualifying key; a tap on an already-active modifier disengages
it (click-to-toggle). Locks are reached only through the Caps Lock key.
.RS
.TP
.B sticky.latch_enabled
bool, default true: quick taps latch the modifier for the next qualifying
key.
.TP
.B sticky.tap_timeout_ms
integer, default 400: maximum press duration for a release to count as a
tap.
.RE
.TP
.B repeat
Type: map. Autorepeat behaviour.
.RS
.TP
.B repeat.enabled
bool, default true: enable autorepeat.
.TP
.B repeat.delay_ms
integer, default 500: delay before repeating.
.TP
.B repeat.cadence_ms
integer, default 30: interval between repeats.
.RE
.TP
.B force_degraded_banner
Type: bool. Default: false. Show the degraded-mode banner even when the
selected backend preserves focus (diagnostics).
.TP
.B text_mode
Type: bool. Default: false. Type characters through the compose/text engine
instead of raw key events. Used by the courts to exercise the text path
deterministically.
.TP
.B terminal
Type: map. The embedded terminal workspace.
.RS
.TP
.B terminal.enabled
bool, default false: activate terminal mode (the
.B \-\-terminal
flag sets this).
.TP
.B terminal.pane_height
integer px, default 420: terminal pane height.
.TP
.B terminal.font_size_px
integer, default 16: terminal font size.
.TP
.B terminal.scrollback_lines
integer, default: the engine's DEFAULT_SCROLLBACK: scrollback capacity in
lines.
.TP
.B terminal.shell
string or null, default null: the child program (null = $SHELL, then
/bin/sh).
.TP
.B terminal.confirm_multiline_paste
bool, default true: require confirmation before pasting multi-line content.
.RE
.TP
.B destination
Type: string. Default: "system". Initial input destination:
.BR system
(keys go to the broker) or
.BR terminal
(keys go to the PTY). The UI can switch destinations at runtime.
.TP
.B adaptive
Type: map. Adaptive key geometry: the OSK learns touch placement and adapts
the effective hit targets while the visible keyboard stays stable. Only
affects touch input; pointer presses keep the exact visual hit-test.
.RS
.TP
.B adaptive.enabled
bool, default true: master switch. When off, touch hit-testing uses the
plain visual rects and no samples are recorded.
.TP
.B adaptive.frozen
bool, default false: freeze the current effective geometry. No learning pass
may mutate it until unfrozen (statistics may still accumulate).
.TP
.B adaptive.min_samples
integer, default 8: minimum samples per key before its hit target may
adapt.
.TP
.B adaptive.optimize_every
integer, default 16: run an optimization pass after this many new samples
(the optimizer never runs on the touch hot path).
.TP
.B adaptive.evidence_confidence
float, default 0.5: maximum normalized-distance confidence below which a
touch counts as an unambiguous intended-key training sample; boundary
touches (ambiguous) never pollute the model.
.RE
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
    layout: us
    view: full
    socket_path: /run/ferrokeyd/ferrokeyd.sock
    width: 920
    height: 342
    sticky:
      latch_enabled: true
      tap_timeout_ms: 400
    repeat:
      enabled: true
      delay_ms: 500
      cadence_ms: 30
    force_degraded_banner: false
    text_mode: false
    terminal:
      enabled: false
      pane_height: 420
      font_size_px: 16
      scrollback_lines: 1000
      shell: null
      confirm_multiline_paste: true
    destination: system
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ferrokey (1),
.BR ferrokeyd.yaml (5),
.BR ferrokeyd (1)
